/*! \mainpage vRTLmod API reference

vRTLmod adds fault injection and differential analysis APIs to Verilator-generated
C++ and SystemC models. This reference covers the common injection interfaces and
the implementation used to analyze, rewrite, and generate model code.

For installation and a runnable first experiment, start with
<a href="https://tum-ei-eda.github.io/vrtlmod/getting-started.html">Get started</a>.
The <a href="https://tum-ei-eda.github.io/vrtlmod/using-vrtlmod.html">user guide</a>
explains target selection, injection timing, and build integration.

\section injection-interfaces Fault injection interfaces

- \ref vrtlfi::td::TD_API "Target dictionary API": prepare faults and look up injection targets.
- \ref vrtlfi::td::TDentry "Target entries": control masks, arming, state access, and injection counters.

\section implementation Implementation

- \ref core.hpp "Core interfaces": coordinate model analysis, target selection, and rewriting.
- \ref vrtlmod::types "Model types": represent modules, variables, cells, and targets.
- \ref vrtlmod::passes "Transformation passes": analyze and rewrite generated C++ through Clang.
- \ref vrtlmod::vapi::VapiGenerator "API generator": emit the injection and differential APIs.

\section reference-index Browse the reference

<a href="annotated.html">Classes</a> &middot;
<a href="namespaces.html">Namespaces</a> &middot;
<a href="files.html">Files</a>
*/
